  "description": "**Epic Summary**\nThis epic builds the Z.immerse immersive editorial experience on the SFCC platform — a dedicated content-led destination that sits alongside the core commerce experience. Z.immerse serves as Zimmermann's digital editorial hub, delivering campaign stories, collection features, and brand content through flexible, visually rich page templates driven by Contentful. The full component scope is subject to design sign-off and is being defined in parallel with this epic.\n\n**Business Value / Objective**\nZ.immerse is central to Zimmermann's brand strategy online — bridging editorial storytelling with product discovery in a way that reflects the brand's premium aesthetic. Delivering a flexible, content-led experience that the Zimmermann team can manage and update through Contentful without code deployment supports the brand's fast-moving seasonal content calendar and elevates the digital experience beyond a standard commerce storefront.\n\n**Scope**\n\n*In Scope*\n\n- Immersive editorial landing page template, consumed from Contentful and rendered via the PWA Kit\n- Direct-link landing page support — Z.immerse pages accessible via direct URL for campaign and marketing use\n- Flexible content component library for editorial page composition, covering layouts to be defined by the Accenture design team in Figma and signed off by Zimmermann; examples include campaign imagery, collection features, editorial copy blocks, and video embeds\n- Contentful content model for Z.immerse page types, enabling the Zimmermann content team to author and publish editorial pages without code deployment\n- Vimeo video embed support on Z.immerse editorial pages via URL stored in Contentful\n\n*Out of Scope*\n\n- Contentful content authoring, editorial content creation, and campaign asset production — Zimmermann responsibility\n- Z.immerse-specific recommendation surfaces (e.g. Recently Viewed on Z.immerse) — TBC pending final designs; if confirmed, covered in SFCC-7 Search & Recommendations\n- GTM/analytics events for Z.immerse page interactions — covered in SFCC-22 SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing\n\n**Dependencies**\n\n- Accenture design team — Z.immerse component definitions and Figma specs are not yet finalised; this epic cannot be fully scoped or built until designs are delivered and signed off by Zimmermann\n- SFCC-2 PWA Kit Components — base component library and design system must be in place before Z.immerse-specific components can be built\n- SFCC-3 Homepage & Navigation — global header and navigation must be in place for Z.immerse pages to render correctly within the storefront shell\n- Contentful — Z.immerse content model must be agreed with the Zimmermann content team before development begins\n\n**Assumptions & Constraints**\n\n- The full list of editorial components required for Z.immerse is not yet defined — scope will be confirmed once Accenture design team delivers signed-off Figma specs\n- All Z.immerse content is authored and managed in Contentful by the Zimmermann team; no SFCC Business Manager authoring is required for this epic\n- Z.immerse pages are content-led and do not require SFCC commerce logic beyond standard product linking from editorial content\n- Sprint is TBD pending design delivery timeline\n\n**Priority:** Medium\n\n**Target Release / Sprint:** 5",
  "status": {
    "name": "To Do",
    "category": "To Do",
    "color": "blue-gray"
  }
}"}

