      "comments": [
        {
          "id": "13562",
          "body": "Hi \n@Jhoan Rose Dela Cruz\n - here's my review, grouped by priority.\nSign-Off Blockers\nBootstrap Status, CMA token as GitHub Actions secret.\n The status is inconsistent: the Bootstrap table has it Complete, but Blockers #5, Open Items #4, and the Setup & Ops runbook (318472193, checklist item 9) all have it Incomplete. Can we confirm the actual state and make it consistent - if the CI CMA secret has genuinely been added, tick it everywhere and update the runbook; if not, mark it Incomplete?\nIntegration Architecture, \"Key behaviours confirmed in 02-contentful.md.\"\n SSR-first fetch, GraphQL, and the publish webhook are listed as current behaviour, and useContentful.ts sits under \"Already built\", but this doesn't hold up against the code: the data hook and the homepage (pages/home/index.tsx) both fetch Contentful content client-side via useEffect, and there's no GraphQL client or webhook receiver anywhere in overrides/ or scripts/. Let's split \"built today\" from \"target architecture (to build)\" so the squad doesn't assume SSR editorial is live.\nBlockers #1, locale count.\n The built and live state is 9: \ncontentfulMapping.generated.ts\n (auto-generated from the live SFCC config) and \nsites.overlay.js\n both resolve to nine distinct locale codes across 8 SFCC sites / 10 PWA sites, matching the Setup & Ops runbook and the TSD's own body text. The \"11\" traces back to the Regional Storefronts PRD (REG-043), which actually lists 11 storefront rows, not 11 locales - two of those rows share a locale code each (en-GB for UK and EU-domestic-EN; en-US for US domestic and the planned US-international site), so even that table only has 9 distinct codes. The 11th row is a dated, real requirement (REG-005, updated 2026-07-10) for a US-international split, but it's still TBC in BM and not yet in sites.overlay.js. Since REG-005 is an active decision, can we get a quick confirm from whoever owns regional config that the locale count won't change before we close Blocker #1 as 9?\nSprint-2 content-types table.\n Two of these belong in later sprints: SFCC-67 (Checkout Trust Messaging) sits under the Checkout Flow & Delivery epic, which is Sprint 4, and SFCC-14 (Returns/Refund) is an Epic, which is Sprint 7 - and as you and Tim both noted, we build to a child story, not the epic. Let's remove both rows from the Sprint-2 table and relocate them: SFCC-67 under Sprint 4, SFCC-14 under Sprint 7 (attaching to its child story once it's raised).\nValidate Before Finalising\nSprint-2 content types.\n You rightly flagged these are assumed, not confirmed (SFCC-82, SFCC-190, SFCC-67 defer their model to stories not yet created; none map to an HPC requirement in 04.1.1). \n@Tim Lavelle\n - you'd mentioned running the Sprint-2 authoring approach by Emma and Dani; is that still the plan, and how would you like us to sequence it before we lock the field sets? In the meantime, Jhoan, let's mark the Sprint-2 types provisional.\nMega Menu fields.\n Design-dependent, as you noted - SFCC-96 needs the Figma spec first (it's flagged DesignDependent in Jira). Let's mark those fields provisional pending the design.\nSpikes and To-Dos to Raise (Not Blocking)\nPLP Inline Grid Insert.\n The ID pattern presents the PLP inject as resolved, but Tim flagged we need to confirm we can inject a Contentful item into the SFCC PLP grid without breaking item counts or pagination. There's already a spike for this area - SFCC-238 (Contentful-to-PWA Kit Product/Category ID Rendering) - let's link it here and confirm it covers the pagination/item-count check, and mark the PLP inject \"pending SFCC-238\" in the meantime.\nPDP Accordion, mixed content.\n Tim raised whether the accordion body can pull SFCC content via a simple SFCC var or needs a dedicated component, and you suggested a spike - there's no card for it yet, so let's raise one (or fold it into SFCC-238's scope) and reference it here.\nMRT-apps section.\n As agreed, we'll scratch this - the MRT app architecture is covered by its own spike, SFCC-237 (MRT Application Architecture Strategy), which Gideon and I will take; we'll link that TSD here once it's done.\nRaise with Leads / POs (Decisions Outside Our Control)\nError Handling & Monitoring, New Relic.\n Two things: (a) it's currently anchored to the Integration Reconciliation working doc, which is a draft and actually lists New Relic as \"Not Required\", so please re-anchor to the \"CDN, eCDN & Security Configuration\" page (339935324), which references the Accenture Observability, Tracing & Security Assurance deck and holds the Log Centre to New Relic streaming checklist; (b) New Relic isn't procured or on the credentials tracker yet - I've already raised procurement with Emma/IT and we're pending their reply, so let's frame the alert policies as \"recommended, pending procurement.\"\n\"What is NOT in Contentful\", product imagery.\n This is asserted as SFCC BM, but it isn't settled: the PWA TSD says imagery is served from Contentful, and the DC002 decision page has no decision recorded yet. \n@Tim Lavelle\n - what's your read on where product imagery lands, and should DC002 be the place we lock it? Jhoan, let's mark it \"pending DC002\" meanwhile rather than stating SFCC BM.\nCache and graceful degradation.\n Since footer and homepage always render from Contentful, a full CDA outage gives a broken bare page, currently noted as \"risk accepted.\" \n@Tim Lavelle\n - you'd raised the cache/invalidation angle here; do you see Contentful as effectively a hard dependency for that chrome, or should we plan a minimal static / last-known-good fallback? Keen on your steer before we lock the degradation stance.\nMinor\n\"Tell No Lies\" link\n (Didomi row and monitoring) currently points back to this page - please repoint it to the actual Tell No Lies/GTM reference or drop the hyperlink.\nNet: items 1 to 4 are the sign-off blockers (plus the Handoff Boundary table, which Tim already flagged [FOR UPDATE] to finalise); 5 and 6 need a design/authoring check; 7 to 9 are spikes and to-dos (SFCC-238 and SFCC-237 already exist); 10 to 12 need a lead or PO call - I've raised 10 with Emma/IT, and 11 and 12 are for Tim's steer.\nCC: \n@Hazel Marie Cacalda",
